#
# Build context exclusions.
#
# Two separate jobs, and it is worth keeping them apart:
#
#   1. Keeping the *image* small. Anything the Dockerfile COPYs is the
#      difference between a cache hit and a cache miss on every code change.
#      app/static/{covers,gallery,uploads} is ~130 MB of user-uploaded images
#      that the image serves from a bind-mount at runtime -- shipping a copy
#      would be both huge and wrong.
#
#   2. Keeping the *build context* small. Docker sends whatever is not ignored
#      to the daemon on every build, so an unignored 383 MB directory costs
#      real time on every single build even though it is never COPYed.
#      graphify-out/ was the largest such directory here.
#
# Note the trailing-slash rules of .dockerignore: a bare `graphify-out` also
# matches a file of that name, which is harmless but imprecise. Directories are
# listed with a trailing slash to say what is meant.

# ── Version control ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.git
.gitignore
.github

# ── Python virtualenvs and interpreters ─────────────────────────────────────
.venv
venv
env/
ENV/
__pycache__
*.py[cod]
*$py.class
*.so
*.egg-info/
.eggs/
build/
dist/
pip-wheel-metadata/

# ── Node / frontend build output ────────────────────────────────────────────
# The frontend is a separate image (deploy/Dockerfile.frontend); the backend
# never needs it, and it is the single largest directory in the repository.
node_modules
frontend
.next
npm-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
pnpm-lock.yaml

# ── Tests, specs and planning documents ─────────────────────────────────────
tests
openspec
benchmark
*.bats
htmlcov
.coverage
.coverage.*
coverage.xml
.pytest_cache
.tox
.nox

# ── Lint / type caches ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# .mypy_cache alone was 69 MB in this repository.
.mypy_cache
.ruff_cache
.pylint.d
.cache

# ── Documentation ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# docs/ontology IS copied into the image (OWL/SHACL schemas are loaded at
# runtime), so the negation below re-admits exactly that subtree.
docs
!docs/ontology

# ── Environments and secrets (CRITICAL) ─────────────────────────────────────
# These must never reach a layer. A secret copied into an image persists in
# every layer and every cache entry even if a later RUN removes it.
.env
.env.*
!.env.test
docker-compose.override.yml
*.pem
*.key
*.crt
*.csr
secrets/
!deploy/**/*.key.example
!deploy/**/*.crt.example

# ── IDE, agents and developer tooling ───────────────────────────────────────
.idea/
.vscode/
.devcontainer
.gemini
.agent
.agents
.pids
# .context is the gitignored planning/notes tree, and openspec/changes is a
# symlink into it.
.context

# ── Knowledge-graph and analysis output ─────────────────────────────────────
# Regenerated by `make codegraph-update` / `make graphify-update`; never read at
# runtime. graphify-out alone was 383 MB.
graphify-out
codegraph-out
.codegraph
.iqoqo-mempalace
mempalace-out

# ── Local caches, scratch and exports ───────────────────────────────────────
# These are bind-mounted into the containers at runtime.
exports
scratch
data
app/static/covers
app/static/gallery
app/static/uploads
logs
*.log
tmp
.tmp

# ── Archives and dumps ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# A stray pg_dump in the tree would otherwise be copied into the image and
# would trip the secret scanner on every build.
*.sql
*.sql.gz
*.dump
*.zip
*.tar.gz
*.tgz
*.bak

# ── Local orchestration overrides ───────────────────────────────────────────
Makefile
docker-compose*.yml
docker-compose*.yaml
!docker-compose.yml
Makefile.*
/Makefile
